{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book","id":1457673,"title":"Asian Changeling book","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-25T19:57:59-07:00","id":1457673,"title":"Asian Changeling book","content":"In a discussion with Shinsoryuu, we both shared our interest in a Changeling book that focused on Asia. This is especially interesting to me, because I was born in Tokyo, Japan and lived and worked in China for three years.<br /> <br /> I would really enjoy a corebook that explored the different legends around Asia, looked at the difference between the Western and Eastern variations of Arcadia and the Hedge, and explored the long historical connection between the East and West.<br /> <br /> One way I did the was through Cathayans; Burmese, Cambodians, Chinese, Koreans, Laotians, Japanese, and Vietnamese the were made the changelings of WESTERN true fae.<br /> <br /> I also remember, the someone had created a court system based on the legends of <b><i>Journey to the West</i></b>.<br /> <br /> How have you guys used Asia lore in your changeling games? I am interested in hearing peoples ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T20:38:11-07:00","id":1457677,"title":"","content":"Less \u2018game\u2019 and more \u2018brainstorming and procrastinating ramblings sitting at the back of my brain.\u2019 I\u2019m writing the below down to save it somewhere other than my grey matter:<br /> <br /> The <b>Four Princes</b> take their name from Sino-Korean Confucian art motifs of the same name. Originally branches of the Directional Courts, during the Joseon dynasty they have inherited and supplanted them. They reigned in Seoul and the Kyongi province, competing with the regional Seasonal Courts of the other provinces. The rivalries continued until Imperial Japan attempted cultural ethnocide on the peninsula in their last throes during WW2, shattering both sides\u2019 power bases. In modern times the two sides have reconciled, but in favor of the Four Princes due to their hegemony over the capital and claims to tradition.<br /> <br /> Each Court claims one of the Princes as their name, honors the Virtue attributed to them, and harvests the emotion at the Root of that virtue according to Korean neo-Confucian philosophy.<br /> The <b>Plum Blossoms Court</b> upholds the Virtue of Compassion, and harvests the Root emotion of Pity. Their Mantles evoke the scent of Asian plum fruits, the gentle eastern wind of spring, growth spurts of wood and grass, and azure hues. <br /> The <b>Orchid Court</b> upholds the Virtue of Propriety, and harvests the Root emotion of Concession. Their Mantles evoke the scent of Asian orchid flowers, the warm southern wind of summer, flames burning with purpose, and vermillion hues. <br /> The <b>Chrysanthemum Court</b> upholds the Virtue of Justice, and harvests the Root emotion of Shame. Their Mantles evoke the scent of chrysanthemum flowers, the refreshing western wind of autumn, the sheen and clanging sound of metal, and white hues. <br /> The <b>Bamboo Court</b> upholds the Virtue of Wisdom, and harvests the Root emotion of Judgment. Their Mantles evoke the scent of bamboo sprouts and snowed earth, the cold northern wind of winter, hidden flows of deep waters, and black hues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  White for Chrysths 08-27-2021, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T21:37:55-07:00","id":1457682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1457677#post1457677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Less \u2018game\u2019 and more \u2018brainstorming and procrastinating ramblings sitting at the back of my brain.\u2019 I\u2019m writing the below down to save it somewhere other than my grey matter:<br /> <br /> The <b>Four Princes</b> take their name from Sino-Korean Confucian art motifs of the same name. Originally branches of the Directional Courts, during the Joseon dynasty they have inherited and supplanted them. They reigned in Seoul and the Kyongi province, competing with the regional Seasonal Courts of the other provinces. The rivalries continued until Imperial Japan attempted cultural ethnocide on the peninsula in their last throes during WW2, shattering both sides\u2019 power bases. In modern times the two sides have reconciled, but in favor of the Four Princes due to their hegemony over the capital and claims to tradition.<br /> <br /> Each Court claims one of the Princes as their name, honors the Virtue attributed to them, and harvests the emotion at the Root of that virtue according to Korean neo-Confucian philosophy.<br /> The <b>Plum Blossoms Court</b> upholds the Virtue of Compassion, and harvests the Root emotion of Pity. Their Mantles evoke the scent of Asian plum fruits, the gentle eastern wind of spring, growth spurts of wood and grass, and azure hues.<br /> The <b>Orchid Court</b> upholds the Virtue of Propriety, and harvests the Root emotion of Concession. Their Mantles evoke the scent of Asian orchid flowers, the warm southern wind of summer, flames burning with purpose, and vermillion hues.<br /> The <b>Chrysanthemum Court</b> upholds the Virtue of Justice, and harvests the Root emotion of Shame. Their Mantles evoke the scent of chrysanthemum flowers, the refreshing western wind of autumn, the sheen and clanging sound of metal, and vermillion hues.<br /> The <b>Bamboo Court</b> upholds the Virtue of Wisdom, and harvests the Root emotion of Judgment. Their Mantles evoke the scent of bamboo sprouts and snowed earth, the cold northern wind of winter, hidden flows of deep waters, and black hues.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I love your ideas! You had mentioned that <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Kaguya-hime of Japanese fame could\u2019ve been a fetch. Is there a chance I could convince you to do a character profile for Kaguya?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T21:48:32-07:00","id":1457683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1457682#post1457682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I love your ideas! You had mentioned that <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Kaguya-hime of Japanese fame could\u2019ve been a fetch. Is there a chance I could convince you to do a character profile for Kaguya?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Not until I reread the 2E core and OAT, I\u2019m afraid. And I\u2019m planning to finish the Chronologues and the Imagineers\u2019 fan expansion/update (Mage) at the very least before I touch anything else.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Kaguya, though, didn\u2019t Changeling 2E mention her at some point? Or was that the \u201c1.5E\u201d ie the \u2018Underhill\u2019 open development materials?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-25T21:55:21-07:00","id":1457684,"title":"","content":"The draft for Changeling society in Japan had courts based on the stuff Kaguya asked her suitors to find. You had:<ul><li>The Court of the Fire Rat, whose emotion is defiance</li> <li>The Court of the Dragon's Jewel, whose emotion is conformity/tradition</li> <li>The Court of the Begging Bowl, whose emotion is harmony/peace</li> </ul>As another reference to Kaguya, the changeling with the highest authority in Honshu is called the Moon Princess. Moon Princesses are always female and also have a Leadership Council that helps communicate the various needs and platforms of regional leaders to her.<br /> <br /> I think the draft for &quot;Japan Lost&quot; can still be found somewhere on this forum, though you may have to dig around a bit to find it. Please keep in mind that it was written around a time when some concepts were different than what ended up in the final corebook (e.g. Huntsmen in the previous drafts were very different than the finalized Huntsmen).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","name":"Shinsoryuu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26495_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T19:00:02-07:00","id":1457750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinsoryuu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1457684#post1457684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The draft for Changeling society in Japan had courts based on the stuff Kaguya asked her suitors to find. You had:<ul><li>The Court of the Fire Rat, whose emotion is defiance</li> <li>The Court of the Dragon's Jewel, whose emotion is conformity/tradition</li> <li>The Court of the Begging Bowl, whose emotion is harmony/peace</li> </ul>As another reference to Kaguya, the changeling with the highest authority in Honshu is called the Moon Princess. Moon Princesses are always female and also have a Leadership Council that helps communicate the various needs and platforms of regional leaders to her.<br /> <br /> I think the draft for &quot;Japan Lost&quot; can still be found somewhere on this forum, though you may have to dig around a bit to find it. Please keep in mind that it was written around a time when some concepts were different than what ended up in the final corebook (e.g. Huntsmen in the previous drafts were very different than the finalized Huntsmen).</div> </div> </div> </div>In Japanese folklore, there is a youkai named Nurarihyon, who is also called &quot;The Supreme Commander of all Monsters.&quot; He leads the night parade of one hundred demons (Hyakki Yako) through the streets of Japan on dark and rainy nights. There is actually a manga based on this myth called <i><b>Nurarihyon no Mago.</b></i><br /> <br /> I think that in the Japanese court system, the <i>Nurarihyon</i> is the emperor of all Changelings in Japan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T19:01:41-07:00","id":1457751,"title":"","content":"If you are interested in doing more research for Japanese changelings and ideas for Japanese changeling courts, I highly recommend Youkai Wiki, which can be found here:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://yokai.fandom.com/wiki/Y%C5%8Dkai_Wiki\" target=\"_blank\">Yokai Wiki | Fandom</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-26T21:17:37-07:00","id":1457754,"title":"","content":"Another source of inspiration for a Changeling chronicle that focused on Japan is <b><i>The Great Youaki War. </i></b>Which is about a young Japanese boy, who discovers that he is chosen to be the years Kirin Rider and must defeat nefarious spirit Yasunori Kato. <br /> <br /> You can watch the movie on youtube here:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZdrAbe9eqC0\" target=\"_blank\">(1) The Great Yokai War (Full Feature w/ English Dub) - YouTube</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T11:53:11-07:00","id":1457804,"title":"","content":"I've definitely used youkai as inspiration for changelings, hobgoblins, and True Fae. It's one of the reasons why I was disappointed we didn't end up with &quot;Japan Lost&quot; as one of the settings in the <i>Changeling The Lost</i> corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26495,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","user":"Shinsoryuu","date":". 08-27-2021, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","name":"Shinsoryuu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26495_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T12:05:19-07:00","id":1457808,"title":"","content":"For those interested in the draft for &quot;Japan Lost&quot; and don't want to search the forums, here is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger\">the link</a><br /> <br /> While some parts of it will require adjustment, most of the writeup is really cool, IMO","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T12:32:52-07:00","id":1457812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1457808#post1457808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those interested in the draft for &quot;Japan Lost&quot; and don't want to search the forums, here is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/964083-changeling-2e-japan-kinda-like-tokyo-only-bigger\">the link</a><br /> <br /> While some parts of it will require adjustment, most of the writeup is really cool, IMO</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed that most of the writeup is pretty cool. I've been using it as inspiration for my own idea of a Japanese changeling society that more matches up with the finalized version of the <i>Changeling The Lost</i> corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","name":"Shinsoryuu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26495_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T14:07:08-07:00","id":1457823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinsoryuu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1457804#post1457804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've definitely used youkai as inspiration for changelings, hobgoblins, and True Fae. It's one of the reasons why I was disappointed we didn't end up with &quot;Japan Lost&quot; as one of the settings in the <i>Changeling The Lost</i> corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would really LOVE to see some of your ideas and would even suggest you turn some of them in<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Maybe, if enough people show their interest, the game developer WILL develop of Japan lost rulebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T17:51:12-07:00","id":1457849,"title":"","content":"Shinsoryuu has mentioned that he has made Hasshaku-Sama into a True Fae in his Changeling chronicles that take place in Japan. I think that some of the old Japanese gods would make interesting True Fae, like the god of storms, Susanoo no Mikoto. Bound to the islands of Japan, he often spirits away Miko (Japanese female hunters) to become his oni concubine. As the brother and enemy of the Sun goddess, Amaterasou, he suffers aggravated damage from sunlight and can not enter shrines dedicated to her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T08:12:36-07:00","id":1457903,"title":"","content":"...You want to make Susano'o, who has <i>agriculture</i> as one of his domains, suffer aggravated damage from sunlight?<br /> <br /> Then again, I'm one to talk, considering I take liberties with mythology as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26495,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","user":"Shinsoryuu","date":". 08-28-2021, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","name":"Shinsoryuu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26495_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T12:40:14-07:00","id":1457919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinsoryuu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1457903#post1457903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...You want to make Susano'o, who has <i>agriculture</i> as one of his domains, suffer aggravated damage from sunlight?<br /> <br /> Then again, I'm one to talk, considering I take liberties with mythology as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good Point, I based it off the fact that he is an antagonist to his sister, Amaterasu. Do you have any suggestions for potential frailties?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T21:30:13-07:00","id":1457952,"title":"","content":"One version of the Susano'o legend mentions that the gods shaved his beard and cut his fingernails and toenails before banishing him with a &quot;divine expulsion.&quot; You could always build a convoluted frailty based on that.<br /> <br /> Or you could have snake venom as part of his frailty. While one of Susano'o's most well-known feats is slaying Yamata no Orochi, keep in mind that his go-to strategy was NOT challenging the serpent/dragon head-on, but instead getting the beast so drunk that it couldn't fight back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","name":"Shinsoryuu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26495_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-28T22:01:15-07:00","id":1457954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinsoryuu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1457952#post1457952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One version of the Susano'o legend mentions that the gods shaved his beard and cut his fingernails and toenails before banishing him with a &quot;divine expulsion.&quot; You could always build a convoluted frailty based on that.<br /> <br /> Or you could have snake venom as part of his frailty. While one of Susano'o's most well-known feats is slaying Yamata no Orochi, keep in mind that his go-to strategy was NOT challenging the serpent/dragon head-on, but instead getting the beast so drunk that it couldn't fight back.</div> </div> </div> </div>] Thankyou for the ideas<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You are clearly very knowledgeable about Asian folklore. I am curious if you have made any new kiths based on myths from Japan, China, Korea, or Vietnam?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T16:45:29-07:00","id":1458007,"title":"","content":"One of the ideas I have used for an Asian American changelings was the idea of <i>Cathayans. </i>These are Burmese, Cambodians, Chinese, Japanese, Koreans, Philippines, Vietnamese, and Laotians that were made the Changelings of <i>WESTERN</i> True Fae. Through these characters, I hoped to explore the long, historical connection between the East and West. This ranged from the colonization of Asian nations by Western powers, mass immigration from China and Japan to the United States during the 19th century, U.S. occupation of Japan after WW2, the Vietnam war, and the swarms of Asian students that came to study at major US universities.<br /> <br /> I also hoped to touch upon historical and folklore that touched upon this connection like <b><i>Madame Butterfly</i></b>. During the Tokugawa era there was a Youkai used for anti-Christian propaganda. It was a mantis that told god the names of people who did not pray correctly to god so they could be killed. My idea is to make this youkai actually a Western racketeer that kidnapped ordinary Japanese for Western Gentry to satisfy their craving and fascination with Asian culture. However, I have forgotten what this Mantis Youkai's name is.<br /> <br /> Does anyone know it's name?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-30T18:07:16-07:00","id":1458096,"title":"","content":"I want to share some more of my thoughts on the interaction between Eastern and Western Changelings and True Fae during colonial times. When the Western powers first began trading and conquering the different regions of Asia, The True Fae of the West discovered that they could not enter or influence the Orient and vise versa for the True Fae of the East. Much to the intial discomfort of Western Changelings, they found they could not access the Hedge, while in Asia/The Orient. However, once European powers began setting up Western districts and which they could live and would only be subject to their own laws, Western changelings discovered that they could access the Western Hedge in these districts. As Westerners began developing a fascination and taste for Asian spices, art, and delicacies, Western Gentry began developing an interest and fascination with the different peoples of Asia. When the European powers began conquering Asia, western racketeers developed an underground slave trade in which they smuggled THOUSANDS of men, women and children Asia into the servitude of the Western Gentry. Some of the Western Courts actually began exchanging Asian peoples for their loved ones the True Fae had taken. This was ESPECIALLY bad among the courts of France, Great Britain, and Germanic States.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-30T20:05:59-07:00","id":1458099,"title":"","content":"Here are some more ideas about the <b><i>Cathayans.</i></b><br /> <br /> <b>The Cathayans</b>are more lost than even most changelings.<br /> <br /> 1. When the Cathayans escapes Arcadia and the Hedge, rather than ending up in their homeland, they find themselves in the West; Europe, North America..If they are lucky, perhaps Australia or Russia.<br /> 2. Because they spent their durance in service to one of the Western Fae, they have developed the mannerisms and social perspectives of Western culture. On top of that, they now speak English, French, or German better than their native language <i>(Cathayans get the bilingual or trilingual merit for free) </i>As such, they are treated with hostility and suspicion by Eastern Changelings.<br /> 3. When a Cathayan returns from the Hedge, they are one of the few types of changelings that LOOK different than their original appearance. This is because their mask and mien now reflects Western biases about Asian peoples and cultures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T17:25:06-07:00","id":1458277,"title":"","content":"I am very fond of the Cathayans, because I enjoy using them to show the strong historical connections between the East and West. I built the different Cathayans based on the historical relationship between the U.S. and different Asian countries. I also use the Cathayans to touch on Western bigotry towards Asian Americans and Asians in general.<br /> <br /> Here is my description of Chinese Cathayans.The irony is that, because imperial China limited the Western barbarians to Canton, the changelings of the West very quickly discovered that they could access the Western hedge in western districts. Just as Western mortals showed a fascination with the China, so was this fascination reflected with the faerie creatures of the West. Changelings from England had come to China, hoping to trade for tea, spices, and porcelain, while changelings from the United States were lured by the Chinese market and a fascination with Chinese cultures. Even the Gentry/True Fae developed the same curiosity and interest their former slaves possessed. For that matter, Chinese men would sale to California to take part in the American gold rush or tried to make their fortunes in U.S. farming and building the Transcontinental railroad. In this way many Chinese found themselves falling into the nets of Western Gentry. Yet in the East, Western businessmen found themselves frustrated by their limited access to the Chinese market and lack of interest in Western goods. So, it was the changeling courts, who first smuggled Opium into China for greater access to the Chinese market and racketeers from the American South who used Opium to lure Chinese men, women, and children into the slavery of Western Fae. After the first Opium War, thousands upon thousands of Chinese were given to Western Gentry for they had gained a taste for Chinese women as their consorts and Chinese men to build their kingdoms in Arcadia. This steady stream was slowed to a trickle, when the Communists took over China and closed it to the West. Though a slow yet steady stream still came from Hong Kong. When Nixon reopened China and Chinese began coming to the West as students and then workers in the United States and Europe. <br /> <br /> The highest concentration of Chinese Cathayans can be found in California, though there are some extremely old and powerful Chinese Cathayans living in solitude throughout North America and Western Europe.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Relations Between Chinese Cathayans and the Western Courts: </i></b>Most Chinese Cathayans join the seasonal courts, THOUGH THEY USE Chinese themes for their season and practice old Chinese traditions associated with the seasons.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Relations Between Chinese Cathayans and Chinese Courts: </i></b>The changeling courts of China treat the Chinese Cathayans with hostility and suspicion. They regard the Cathayans as corrupted/tainted, and no longer true Mandarins yet not truly Americans, either. Ironically, they still consider them Chinese and under Chinese law. The Western Courts have tried to use Chinese Cathayans as a bridge between them and the Chinese courts, yet this does not go well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T17:48:12-07:00","id":1458431,"title":"","content":"<b><i>Japanese Cathayans: </i></b>Because the Japanese very quickly adapted to Western technology and political structure, from the end of the Tokugawa period to the beginning of WW2, there was never the steady stream of Japanese disappearing into the slavery of Western Gentry like other Asian societies; Burma, Cambodia, China, India, Laos, and Vietnam. Though a handful of Japanese disappeared each year. This DID NOT protect the Japanese who immigrated to Hawaii, Europe, and the mainland United States, with several thousand disappearing into Western Arcadia from 1868 to 1911. After the devastation of WW2 and the United States occupied Japan, the chaos allowed many American racketeers to capture and ship thousands more to Western Arcadia. Japanese students also made tempting targets for US loyalists and racketeers. After the year 2000, the number of Japanese disappearing into Western arcadia has become a slow but steady drip, drip, drip. Although the number of Japanese immigrating to the US to study or work has shrunk, because of Japanese media, there is still a strong interest in Japan from Western Gentry. While it is dangerous, there are organizations of US racketeers posing as western businessmen in Japan to kidnap Japanese girls and women to be consorts for the Western Gentry.<br /> The largest populations of Japanese Cathayans can be found in Brazil, Hawaii, California, Oregon, and Washington, though Japanese Cathayans can be found in Canada, Mexico, and Europe. Interestingly, the US population of Japanese Cathayans is disproportionally large in regards to the Japanese American population. This is due to a combination of the longevity the wyrd provides and some Japanese Cathayans have not officially become US citizens even if they have lived in the US for decades or more than a century.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Relations Between Japanese Cathayans and Western Courts: </i></b>Like Chinese Cathayans, most Japanese Cathayans join the seasonal courts, but with Japanese themes and rituals. Interestingly, Japanese Cathayans tend to be more traditional than most modern Japanese. This is especially true in Hawaii.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Relations Between Japanese Cathayans and the Japanese Courts: </i></b>Unlike the Chinese, the Japanese and Japanese Cathayans get along pretty well. However, the Japanese courts do not consider the Cathayans true Japanese anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T19:13:22-07:00","id":1458437,"title":"","content":"Please, please, do not use the word &quot;Cathayans&quot; here. This is an archaic word used during a period when Europeans knew little about what was going on in central and eastern Asia, derived from the Khitan of northern China and misattributed to other territories of China. Referring to people from Japan or Korea as Cathayans is like referring to Peru as &quot;the East Indies&quot; or to the Spanish and the Irish as &quot;vikings.&quot; Korea in particular has a history of resisting foreign invasions, including by the Khitan specifically. It is kind of rude to call them Chinese people.<br /> <br /> I am just very uncomfortable with this idea of &quot;Cathayan Lost&quot; as explicitly in-world stereotyped peoples in general, and it really distracts from the evocative myths you can draw on that might reflect East Asian interpretations of something like the Durance. Why does Urashima Taro have to run around in cosmically imposed yellowface? He's already got enough to deal with guarding the treasure box that contains the three hundred years that passed on Earth while he was in the Dragon Palace under the ocean depths. If you want to explore themes of human prejudice, do it by having humans show prejudice, not by having the universe itself single out Asian people and displace and literally otherize them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T19:33:51-07:00","id":1458438,"title":"","content":"Was going to say something after putting all together, but Stupid Loserman pretty much said it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T21:00:26-07:00","id":1458448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458438#post1458438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was going to say something after putting all together, but Stupid Loserman pretty much said it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I understand what you guys mean, sorry<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> One themes I wanted to touch upon with the characters was Western biases and racism towards peoples of Asia. I chose the term Cathayan, because it was the term the Kindred <i>(Vampire: The Masquerade)</i> used for the Kue-jin from <i>Kindred of the East.</i> I should have done more research on the term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T21:04:47-07:00","id":1458449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458437#post1458437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, please, do not use the word &quot;Cathayans&quot; here. This is an archaic word used during a period when Europeans knew little about what was going on in central and eastern Asia, derived from the Khitan of northern China and misattributed to other territories of China. Referring to people from Japan or Korea as Cathayans is like referring to Peru as &quot;the East Indies&quot; or to the Spanish and the Irish as &quot;vikings.&quot; Korea in particular has a history of resisting foreign invasions, including by the Khitan specifically. It is kind of rude to call them Chinese people.<br /> <br /> I am just very uncomfortable with this idea of &quot;Cathayan Lost&quot; as explicitly in-world stereotyped peoples in general, and it really distracts from the evocative myths you can draw on that might reflect East Asian interpretations of something like the Durance. Why does Urashima Taro have to run around in cosmically imposed yellowface? He's already got enough to deal with guarding the treasure box that contains the three hundred years that passed on Earth while he was in the Dragon Palace under the ocean depths. If you want to explore themes of human prejudice, do it by having humans show prejudice, not by having the universe itself single out Asian people and displace and literally otherize them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do you guys have any suggestions? I really want to touch upon the biases and bigotry many Asian-Europeans and Asian Americans have gone and are currently going through. I am embarrased at how thoughtless I was on using that term, and I want to emphasize that these characters are just as much Americans or Europeans as the Caucasian changelings and characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T21:27:22-07:00","id":1458451,"title":"","content":"Eh, it could be just an in-universe slang/slur among the people, as it was in real life. Changelings are still people after all, and creative dickery is one of the things that people outdo the Gentry in.<br /> <br /> Social Conditions probably work better. Like Ergi in Dark Eras (or whatever the name was for that Condition where you were penalized for being unmanly).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 09-03-2021, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T21:42:30-07:00","id":1458453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458448#post1458448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I chose the term Cathayan, because it was the term the Kindred <i>(Vampire: The Masquerade)</i> used for the Kue-jin from <i>Kindred of the East.</i> I should have done more research on the term.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figured that's where it probably came from. It was a weird pull when Kindred of the East did it, and one of a lot of things Kindred of the East did that were, if not outright offensive or insensitive, then clumsy at best. It is not a good model to aspire to.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure exactly what you're trying to do in this thread: brainstorm ideas for a fanbook you're writing? Pitch structural elements for a game you're going to play in? Just spitball cool ways you imagine the courts of the Lost might manifest in the countries of East Asia?<br /> <br /> My advice would be to stay grounded, and to write what you know.<br /> <br /> Stay grounded: Don't write material about <b>Asian</b> Lost, write material about Asian <b>Lost.</b> One of the strengths of Lost as a game is the wide breadth of ways in which the world of the fae manifests, and that variety isn't going to be diminished in other parts of the world. Another strength is Lost's potential to focus on relatable human drama. People are people, not just manifestations of the culture they live in. Go anywhere and you'll find rebels, hotheads, the meek, the cold, technocrats, traditionalists, pragmatists, the self-sacrificing and the selfish. Cultures are just circumstances these people find themselves in and navigate. Consequentially, writing a sub-template about specific types of Eastern Lost that manifests differently from Western Lost is missing the universality and the relatable humanness of the concept. Alternate Court structures don't hit this problem nearly as much; a different court structure is simply a different framing in which these human dramas play out, deriving from local historical circumstances and whatever bargains have been struck with patrons who might deal with the Lost. Avoid being monolithic, though. You're not going to have &quot;these are the courts of Japan&quot; or &quot;this is the ruler of the Japanese Lost&quot; any more than you have &quot;these are the courts of the United States&quot; or &quot;this is the reigning leader of the American Lost.&quot; The corebook already contains examples of how the seasonal courts are not universal. New Orleans has the Traders' Courts and Ipswitch on the New England coast has the Courts of the Tides. Changeling society is locally focused and has a lot of variations.<br /> <br /> Write what you know: If you don't know what life looks like for a person living in Japan enough to portray an image of it, either don't write about it, or do research until that changes before you do write about it. If you feel more comfortable writing about the Asian-American or Asian-European experience, write that. A first-generation immigrant is going to have a very different outlook from a third or even second generation mixed-race Asian-American who was born in the States speaking English from childhood. If that's the story you're writing about, the court structure overseas probably doesn't have a lot of direct relevance. Even a first-generation immigrant who moves to the West before suffering the Durance isn't going to know anything about how the Lost organize themselves in their home country until they either start corresponding online or take a trip back home and encounter them.<br /> <br /> Just in general, it's a good idea to step back and clearly identify for what purpose you're writing. When you have a clear idea of whether you're writing &quot;game elements for use in a story in an American city with a large Asian demographic&quot; or &quot;sample courts and characters in a domain of Lost in modern Shenzhen facing the reawakening of a Wild Hunt long forestalled and forgotten,&quot; it's a lot easier to narrow down resources to draw research from, to outline particular topics you should address and elucidate on, and for others to provide you with advice and ideas on where to go, as opposed to the vague and broad prompt of &quot;Changeling in East Asia: ideas?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T21:56:39-07:00","id":1458456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458453#post1458453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I figured that's where it probably came from. It was a weird pull when Kindred of the East did it, and one of a lot of things Kindred of the East did that were, if not outright offensive or insensitive, then clumsy at best. It is not a good model to aspire to.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure exactly what you're trying to do in this thread: brainstorm ideas for a fanbook you're writing? Pitch structural elements for a game you're going to play in? Just spitball cool ways you imagine the courts of the Lost might manifest in the countries of East Asia?<br /> <br /> My advice would be to stay grounded, and to write what you know.<br /> <br /> Stay grounded: Don't write material about <b>Asian</b> Lost, write material about Asian <b>Lost.</b> One of the strengths of Lost as a game is the wide breadth of ways in which the world of the fae manifests, and that variety isn't going to be diminished in other parts of the world. Another strength is Lost's potential to focus on relatable human drama. People are people, not just manifestations of the culture they live in. Go anywhere and you'll find rebels, hotheads, the meek, the cold, technocrats, traditionalists, pragmatists, the self-sacrificing and the selfish. Cultures are just circumstances these people find themselves in and navigate. Consequentially, writing a sub-template about specific types of Eastern Lost that manifests differently from Western Lost is missing the universality and the relatable humanness of the concept. Alternate Court structures don't hit this problem nearly as much; a different court structure is simply a different framing in which these human dramas play out, deriving from local historical circumstances and whatever bargains have been struck with patrons who might deal with the Lost. Avoid being monolithic, though. You're not going to have &quot;these are the courts of Japan&quot; or &quot;this is the ruler of the Japanese Lost&quot; any more than you have &quot;these are the courts of the United States&quot; or &quot;this is the reigning leader of the American Lost.&quot; The corebook already contains examples of how the seasonal courts are not universal. New Orleans has the Traders' Courts and Ipswitch on the New England coast has the Courts of the Tides. Changeling society is locally focused and has a lot of variations.<br /> <br /> Write what you know: If you don't know what life looks like for a person living in Japan enough to portray an image of it, either don't write about it, or do research until that changes before you do write about it. If you feel more comfortable writing about the Asian-American or Asian-European experience, write that. A first-generation immigrant is going to have a very different outlook from a third or even second generation mixed-race Asian-American who was born in the States speaking English from childhood. If that's the story you're writing about, the court structure overseas probably doesn't have a lot of direct relevance. Even a first-generation immigrant who moves to the West before suffering the Durance isn't going to know anything about how the Lost organize themselves in their home country until they either start corresponding online or take a trip back home and encounter them.<br /> <br /> Just in general, it's a good idea to step back and clearly identify for what purpose you're writing. When you have a clear idea of whether you're writing &quot;game elements for use in a story in an American city with a large Asian demographic&quot; or &quot;sample courts and characters in a domain of Lost in modern Shenzhen facing the reawakening of a Wild Hunt long forestalled and forgotten,&quot; it's a lot easier to narrow down resources to draw research from, to outline particular topics you should address and elucidate on, and for others to provide you with advice and ideas on where to go, as opposed to the vague and broad prompt of &quot;Changeling in East Asia: ideas?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What I was hoping to accomplish was have people share some of their ideas for Asian changeling chronicles that could potentially inspire an idea for a Changeling corebook that focused on Asia. There are alot of myths and legends that players might not be aware of and I was hoping people could share some of their ideas. With the Changeling Asian American characters, I was trying to show the long and historical connections between the East and West, as well as the Wests fascination with Asia, particularly China and Japan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T21:59:01-07:00","id":1458457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458451#post1458451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, it could be just an in-universe slang/slur among the people, as it was in real life. Changelings are still people after all, and creative dickery is one of the things that people outdo the Gentry in.<br /> <br /> Social Conditions probably work better. Like Ergi in Dark Eras (or whatever the name was for that Condition where you were penalized for being unmanly).</div> </div> </div> </div>What I am trying to capture with the characters is the Wests' fascination, resentment, with the East and how Asians have become an important part of American culture, as well as our long historical connections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T22:27:41-07:00","id":1458462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458451#post1458451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Social Conditions probably work better. Like Ergi in Dark Eras (or whatever the name was for that Condition where you were penalized for being unmanly).</div> </div> </div> </div>That could work. Part of the problem is that Asian Americans tend to think of themselves as distinct groups, like Nikkei for Japanese Americans, or just Chinese Americans for Americans from China (<i>Note: The Chinese refer to Chinese Americans as Meiguo Chusheng Huayi)</i> with the term Asian American given to them by 1960s college students.<br /> <br /> Also, they are distinct from the Changelings courts of Asia who immigrated to the West in that they are Asian peoples made changelings by Western Gentry and, unfortunately, reflect biases of Asians in their masks and miens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T22:34:14-07:00","id":1458464,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Just a phenomenon where the Hedgeways and Trods go crazy and start dumping Asian changelings to Europe and vice-versa would cause a lot of fascination (\u201cOoh, exotic.\u201d \u201cCould they be our allies?\u201d \u201cHey how do you do Contracts and bargains there?\u201d) and resentment (\u201cIs it an invasion?\u201d \u201cHow can we trust them?\u201d \u201cWe don\u2019t have Hollows, Trods and Glamour to spare to these vagrants.\u201d)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T22:40:27-07:00","id":1458465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458462#post1458462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, they are distinct from the Changelings courts of Asia who immigrated to the West in that they are Asian peoples made changelings by Western Gentry and, unfortunately, <b>reflect biases of Asians in their masks and miens.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm, not exactly a subject to publicly brainstorm about\u2026<br /> <br /> If I was doing it, I\u2019ll say that it\u2019s not the Gentry\u2019s work \u2014 they\u2019re too distant and uncaring for that. I feel they\u2019re more likely to just straight up represent themselves as the mythological figures themselves. <br /> <br /> Rather, it\u2019s a group of Asian changelings themselves (be they natural immigrants, or Hedge-stranded) who obfuscate their intentions and exact identities with such blatant self-ridicule. The dirty \u2018Chinese\u2019 (locals not caring about whether he\u2019s really Chinese or not) waiter who speaks in pidgin English is unlikely to be suspected as the true identity of the eloquent masked gentleman with a thick British accent who runs the local Goblin Market.<br /> <br /> The other Asian changelings who aren\u2019t in on it are, naturally, pissed off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 09-03-2021, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T22:49:04-07:00","id":1458466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458464#post1458464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Just a phenomenon where the Hedgeways and Trods go crazy and start dumping Asian changelings to Europe and vice-versa would cause a lot of fascination (\u201cOoh, exotic.\u201d \u201cCould they be our allies?\u201d \u201cHey how do you do Contracts and bargains there?\u201d) and resentment (\u201cIs it an invasion?\u201d \u201cHow can we trust them?\u201d \u201cWe don\u2019t have Hollows, Trods and Glamour to spare to these vagrants.\u201d)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Initialy, when the Western Changelings came to Asia, they found that they could not enter the Hedge. For that matter, the True Fae's power and influence was limited to the region they represented. However, once the European Imperials powers began setting up Western districts and territories in the different regions of Asia, they found that they could enter the WESTERN hedge. Even better, the Changelings and Courts of Asia could not follow them. During imperial times, Loyalists and racketeers used this to set up a slave trade from Asia.<br /> <br /> In modern times, the worm has turned, somewhat. The Courts of Asia can use the EASTERN hedge to travel to Asian districts in the Wests and have used this to establish themselves in the North America, Europe, and Australia","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T22:52:42-07:00","id":1458467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458465#post1458465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mmm, not exactly a subject to publicly brainstorm about\u2026<br /> <br /> If I was doing it, I\u2019ll say that it\u2019s not the Gentry\u2019s work \u2014 they\u2019re too distant and uncaring for that. I feel they\u2019re more likely to just straight up represent themselves as the mythological figures themselves.<br /> <br /> Rather, it\u2019s a group of Asian changelings themselves (be they natural immigrants, or Hedge-stranded) who obfuscate their intentions and exact identities with such blatant self-ridicule. The dirty \u2018Chinese\u2019 (locals not caring about whether he\u2019s really Chinese or not) waiter who speaks in pidgin English is unlikely to be suspected as the true identity of the eloquent masked gentleman with a thick British accent who runs the local Goblin Market.<br /> <br /> The other Asian changelings who aren\u2019t in on it are, naturally, pissed off.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What I envision is that it is somewhat represented in the seeming they are given. Asians are portrayed as diligent and hard working, so many Asian men are given they Wizened seeming. They are also portrayed as sneaky and treacherous, so Asian men are also given the darkling seeming.<br /> <br /> Asian women are regarded as submissive and hyper sexed so they almost always are given the fairest seeming and return with the Striking Looks merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T23:04:09-07:00","id":1458468,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not so sure about the culturally segregated Hedge thing \u2014 circumstances like that are rare, if any, in the CofD. A \u201cthere be dragons\u201d line on the map being drawn because the locals there not caring about bargains you made on this side of the map feels more likely.<br /> <br /> <br /> And the Seemings\u2026 er\u2026 isn\u2019t that still along the lines of \u201cDude, are we <i>sure</i> we\u2019re doing this?\u201d we mentioned earlier?<br /> I mean, there\u2019s a difference between \u201cWell what do you know, some folks do fit the stereotype\u201d and \u201cThe stereotype is being perpetuated by the powers-that-are.\u201d Maybe some infamous Asian Darkling and his Fairest Wife made a notorious name for themselves like Bonnie and Clyde or something in the backstory, but suggesting a broad stroke in that direction feels\u2026 off.<br /> <br /> And not just about the racism/Orientalism stuff \u2014 Seemings 2E iirc are about both what the Gentry inflicts on a person, and how that persons turns it around to make an escape. Why would the Strangers care so much about the Asian and European cultural stereotypes, and can they even care in the first place? And why would the changelings-to-be see a need to conform to such stereotypes in their oh-god-I-have-to-run desperate escape?<br /> <br /> <br /> Gotta go somewhere now; will come back if I have any thing else to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-02T23:23:07-07:00","id":1458471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458468#post1458468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not so sure about the culturally segregated Hedge thing \u2014 circumstances like that are rare, if any, in the CofD. A \u201cthere be dragons\u201d line on the map being drawn because the locals there not caring about bargains you made on this side of the map feels more likely.<br /> <br /> <br /> And the Seemings\u2026 er\u2026 isn\u2019t that still along the lines of \u201cDude, are we <i>sure</i> we\u2019re doing this?\u201d we mentioned earlier?<br /> I mean, there\u2019s a difference between \u201cWell what do you know, some folks do fit the stereotype\u201d and \u201cThe stereotype is being perpetuated by the powers-that-are.\u201d Maybe some infamous Asian Darkling and his Fairest Wife made a notorious name for themselves like Bonnie and Clyde or something in the backstory, but suggesting a broad stroke in that direction feels\u2026 off.<br /> <br /> And not just about the racism/Orientalism stuff \u2014 Seemings 2E iirc are about both what the Gentry inflicts on a person, and how that persons turns it around to make an escape. Why would the Strangers care so much about the Asian and European cultural stereotypes, and can they even care in the first place? And why would the changelings-to-be see a need to conform to such stereotypes in their oh-god-I-have-to-run desperate escape?<br /> <br /> <br /> Gotta go somewhere now; will come back if I have any thing else to say.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A main theme of Changeling the Lost is overcoming the identity forced on you by your Keeper. Part of the immigrant experience is suffering, but also overcoming that to succeed. I wanted to combine both for these characters. I also wanted to touch upon historical event and conflict between the East and West which, unfortunately, it is ripe with racism, exploitation.<br /> <br /> Also, Your seeming isn't your true identity, but the one forced on you by your Keeper. Being made a darkling did not necessarily mean you were a bad person or a criminal, it is just the role your Keeper gave you while in Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T00:24:05-07:00","id":1458476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458471#post1458471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A main theme of Changeling the Lost is overcoming the identity forced on you by your Keeper. Part of the immigrant experience is suffering, but also overcoming that to succeed. I wanted to combine both for these characters. I also wanted to touch upon historical event and conflict between the East and West which, unfortunately, it is ripe with racism, exploitation.<br /> <br /> Also, Your seeming isn't your true identity, but the one forced on you by your Keeper. Being made a darkling did not necessarily mean you were a bad person or a criminal, it is just the role your Keeper gave you while in Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I agree \u2014 it\u2019s just that I think tying those ideas to core template mechanics is a rather risky proposition. Like, there was some talk when one of the Dark Eras (for Tokyo) suggested a connection between Ainu and werewolves/Wolf-Blooded. I don\u2019t quite clearly remember how it was resolved, but I believe it was something like an in-universe bias/misperception. Things like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T00:28:50-07:00","id":1458477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458471#post1458471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A main theme of Changeling the Lost is overcoming the identity forced on you by your Keeper. Part of the immigrant experience is suffering, but also overcoming that to succeed. I wanted to combine both for these characters. I also wanted to touch upon historical event and conflict between the East and West which, unfortunately, it is ripe with racism, exploitation.<br /> <br /> Also, Your seeming isn't your true identity, but the one forced on you by your Keeper. Being made a darkling did not necessarily mean you were a bad person or a criminal, it is just the role your Keeper gave you while in Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know from other threads that this is how you prefer to envision and play Changeling: The Lost, but it's not a universal take on it. In the game Seemings are enforced by your experiences in Arcadia (which ultimately do derive from your Keeper) but are also very wide and generslly without any specific descriptors (Beasts and Elementals being exceptions, as they are assumed by the game to be based on a single animal or element). Kiths are what grants specificity and is the big factor in determining things such as your Mien, but Kiths are only sometimes forced upon changelings by Gentry; many times they're gained because of other reasons not directly related to their Keepers.<br /> <br /> I also think a lot of players (maybe not your own players, but others who'd read this theoretical book) won't appreciate how much you make their Keepers influences their characters. It's also weird to me how all Keepers tend to enforce the same specific roles based on human stereotypes when Gentry are supposed both diverse and alien.<br /> Yeah, they do conform to ideas that'd fit into human folklore to a large degree, but any roles they enforce on their &quot;wards&quot; are according to their own alien desires and not according to six specific archetypes that apparently all True Fae have a desire to emulate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T06:35:08-07:00","id":1458504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458476#post1458476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I agree \u2014 it\u2019s just that I think tying those ideas to core template mechanics is a rather risky proposition. Like, there was some talk when one of the Dark Eras (for Tokyo) suggested a connection between Ainu and werewolves/Wolf-Blooded. I don\u2019t quite clearly remember how it was resolved, but I believe it was something like an in-universe bias/misperception. Things like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was Olivia Hill's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=958058#post958058\">sample setting</a> for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/957036-forsaken-and-the-ainu?p=958220#post958220\">Werewolf 2e</a>. I vaguely recall (but, of course, cannot find the thread for) it being based on a real-world topic of modern Japanese genetics/ancestry as it relates to the Ainu people, which itself seems to go back to Japan having been home to two (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genetic_history_of_East_Asians#Genetic_history_of_Japanese\" target=\"_blank\">to simplify greatly</a>) different ethnotypes way back in the archipelago's history.<br /> <br /> And yeah, it's extremely weird to suppose Keepers will consistently tie racial/ethnic/national stereotypes to the associated group of people when they don't even consistently do that for sex and gender. The nearest the game has historically done in that direction is to give specific Keepers preferred territories to interact with, and that's going to have the opposite effect from reproducing &quot;this is specifically how human foreigners view this group.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T06:44:21-07:00","id":1458505,"title":"","content":"Of course, what I and others here say don\u2019t mean \u201cThis is wrong and don\u2019t do it\u201d \u2014 I\u2019d in fact like to see how this all gets hammered into shape. Likely, some strange Courtly customs and Pledges being thrown around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T14:08:17-07:00","id":1458567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458505#post1458505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, what I and others here say don\u2019t mean \u201cThis is wrong and don\u2019t do it\u201d \u2014 I\u2019d in fact like to see how this all gets hammered into shape. Likely, some strange Courtly customs and Pledges being thrown around.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To give you an idea of what I am envisioning, here is one of the npc characters and am building for the chronicle.<br /> <br /> <i>Madame Butterfly</i> is a Nikkei Fairest Nightsinger and the inspiration for Pierre Loti\u2019s Madame Chrysantheme, Jon Long\u2019s short story <i>Madame Butterfly, </i>and Puccini\u2019s opera of the same name. In 1858, she was a young geisha named Kiku Aikawa, she was lured by an American naval office, who was also a changeling racketeer from the Winter Court, who married her and then sold her to one of the Western Gentry. This was actually a common tactic used by American loyalists to kidnap and she Japanese women to the Western True Fae. When escaped the Hedge, she found herself in San Francisco in the year 1903, where she became a popular opera singer for, ironically, <i>Madame Butterfly. </i>She used her popularity as an opera singer to help win concessions for the Japanese American and Nikkei changelings. After the 1906, San Francisco earthquake, she helped set up the Nikkei freehold in South Park. By 1912, she had become the Spring Queen in Japan Town. In modern times, she acts as a mediator between the seasonal courts and the courts of Japan.<br /> <b><i>Appearance: </i></b>Despite being a centurion, she still looks like a beautiful young woman in her early twenties. This is due to a combination of being a wyrd 8 changeling and having the long of days merit. Her skin a very pale and baby, smooth, and her hair is a magnificent main of black. Behind the mask, her mien as moonlight on snow white skin, pointed ears, deep purple eyes, and her hair is many different tones of black.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T14:12:01-07:00","id":1458568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458477#post1458477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know from other threads that this is how you prefer to envision and play Changeling: The Lost, but it's not a universal take on it. In the game Seemings are enforced by your experiences in Arcadia (which ultimately do derive from your Keeper) but are also very wide and generslly without any specific descriptors (Beasts and Elementals being exceptions, as they are assumed by the game to be based on a single animal or element). Kiths are what grants specificity and is the big factor in determining things such as your Mien, but Kiths are only sometimes forced upon changelings by Gentry; many times they're gained because of other reasons not directly related to their Keepers.<br /> <br /> I also think a lot of players (maybe not your own players, but others who'd read this theoretical book) won't appreciate how much you make their Keepers influences their characters. It's also weird to me how all Keepers tend to enforce the same specific roles based on human stereotypes when Gentry are supposed both diverse and alien.<br /> Yeah, they do conform to ideas that'd fit into human folklore to a large degree, but any roles they enforce on their &quot;wards&quot; are according to their own alien desires and not according to six specific archetypes that apparently all True Fae have a desire to emulate.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Keeper doesn't enforce the same role on ALL their Asian changelings, but they DO build them on Western biases AND what brought them to the West.<br /> <br /> Such as, there is a character whom is Chinese an came to California for the gold rush, so his keeper made him a wizened miner, another Changeling is a Chinese who helped build the transcontinental railroad, so HIS Keeper made him a wizened artists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T15:01:10-07:00","id":1458573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458568#post1458568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Keeper doesn't enforce the same role on ALL their Asian changelings, but they DO build them on Western biases AND what brought them to the West.<br /> <br /> Such as, there is a character whom is Chinese an came to California for the gold rush, so his keeper made him a wizened miner, another Changeling is a Chinese who helped build the transcontinental railroad, so HIS Keeper made him a wizened artists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Why do they subscribe to outdated human stereotypes or exclusively take Western perspectives? Why aren't there True Fae styled after actual East Asian folklore? Why aren't there Keepers who just don't give a shit about their victims' ethnicities? (I would personally assume the latter is far more common.)<br /> What is the purpose of making all American Gentry (as much as any Gentry are associated with any earthly location) have these specific views?<br /> <br /> What force is there that makes American Keepers behave in this uniform manner when it comes to victims of Asian descent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T16:24:45-07:00","id":1458580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458573#post1458573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why? Why do they subscribe to outdated human stereotypes or exclusively take Western perspectives? Why aren't there True Fae styled after actual East Asian folklore? Why aren't there Keepers who just don't give a shit about their victims' ethnicities? (I would personally assume the latter is far more common.)<br /> What is the purpose of making all American Gentry (as much as any Gentry are associated with any earthly location) have these specific views?<br /> <br /> What force is there that makes American Keepers behave in this uniform manner when it comes to victims of Asian descent?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There ARE True Fae styles after Asian Folklore and mythology. I think Raijin, Fujin, and Susanoo would make interesting True Fae. The changelings I am describing were spirited away by Western loyalists/racketeers or taken when they immigrated to the US.<br /> <br /> Also...the Wizened I mentioned you spirited away during the 1840s, which is why they are portrayed on old stereotypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T17:16:53-07:00","id":1458584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458573#post1458573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why? Why do they subscribe to outdated human stereotypes or exclusively take Western perspectives? Why aren't there True Fae styled after actual East Asian folklore? Why aren't there Keepers who just don't give a shit about their victims' ethnicities? (I would personally assume the latter is far more common.)<br /> What is the purpose of making all American Gentry (as much as any Gentry are associated with any earthly location) have these specific views?<br /> <br /> What force is there that makes American Keepers behave in this uniform manner when it comes to victims of Asian descent?</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to give more thoughts on my ideas for Western and Eastern True Fae. True Fae are given material form by the folklore, legends, and myths they represent. This limited the ability of EASTERN true Fae to influence the West and Vise versa for Western True Fae. It ALSO limited changelings abilities to access the hedge. Time and Space in the Hedge and Arcadia are controlled by the oaths and pledges of the specific beliefs, customs, and traditions of the nations/regions are a reflection of, which affects a changelings portaling abilities. When Europe rediscovered Asia and began trading with the region, Western changelings initially found that they could not portal while in Asia. However, when the imperial European powers began setting up colonies and Western territories in Asia, the Western courts and that they could enter the Western hedge from these districts. Even better, the Eastern courts could not follow them. The worm turned, when the Chinese, Japanese, and Koreans began setting up Eastern districts in North America and Western Europe. They were still LIMITED, however, by the lack of influence the Eastern cultures had in the West. This changed in the Late 90's and 2000s.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T17:59:06-07:00","id":1458590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458584#post1458584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True Fae are given material form by the folklore, legends, and myths they represent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this the position you're consciously taking to move the game into the idea space you're trying to move into, or is this the assumption you're starting from about the game that is influencing what idea space you see it moving into?<br /> <br /> If the latter, this is the point of disagreement. If the former, I still disagree with this move in terms of whether it plays well to Changeling's themes, but it's at least a conscious decision to change matters towards a specific end, and I respect that much.<br /> <br /> There's some room for interpretation, but this element of narrative design, in my opinion, best belongs on a higher layer up from the diegetic. In terms of you and I telling stories to each other about fictional changelings, yes, the True Fae take direct inspiration from folklore and myth about alien beings and places of both wonder and terror (both traditional <i>and</i> modern; remember that Changeling accepts UFO abduction stories as being of a kind with premodern tales about faerie lords spiriting people away). That's not literalized within the setting. The True Fae are not made of stories humans tell one another. Rather, humans sometimes tell one another stories (at one or two or three levels of remove from the moment of contact and inspiration) <i>about</i> the True Fae. They are alien gods. Aesthetically, yes, from a narrative design standpoint, they are also dragons and princes and devils and enmas. But they aren't paper tigers or creative hollows humanity unconsciously creates through their subconscious fears. They sometimes deign to wear the trappings of human cultures, but this is an affectation, almost a diversion for them.<br /> <br /> It's okay if you don't agree with me stating it this strongly; again, there's room for interpretation. But Changeling isn't a game about physical manifestations of culture concepts where changing the idea landscape changes the enemy. I think it would be a different game if it were that (and there are other games that are more like what that is). It would be less personal and more zoomed out and ideological. The fundamental focus is on the relationship between changeling and Keeper, not between culture and Faerie. Culture is relevant because it is important to <i>human</i> life and speaks to what ties the Lost to the people around them ironside. To the Strangers, human life is just another performance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T18:14:35-07:00","id":1458593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458590#post1458590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this the position you're consciously taking to move the game into the idea space you're trying to move into, or is this the assumption you're starting from about the game that is influencing what idea space you see it moving into?<br /> <br /> If the latter, this is the point of disagreement. If the former, I still disagree with this move in terms of whether it plays well to Changeling's themes, but it's at least a conscious decision to change matters towards a specific end, and I respect that much.<br /> <br /> There's some room for interpretation, but this element of narrative design, in my opinion, best belongs on a higher layer up from the diegetic. In terms of you and I telling stories to each other about fictional changelings, yes, the True Fae take direct inspiration from folklore and myth about alien beings and places of both wonder and terror (both traditional <i>and</i> modern; remember that Changeling accepts UFO abduction stories as being of a kind with premodern tales about faerie lords spiriting people away). That's not literalized within the setting. The True Fae are not made of stories humans tell one another. Rather, humans sometimes tell one another stories (at one or two or three levels of remove from the moment of contact and inspiration) <i>about</i> the True Fae. They are alien gods. Aesthetically, yes, from a narrative design standpoint, they are also dragons and princes and devils and enmas. But they aren't paper tigers or creative hollows humanity unconsciously creates through their subconscious fears. They sometimes deign to wear the trappings of human cultures, but this is an affectation, almost a diversion for them.<br /> <br /> It's okay if you don't agree with me stating it this strongly; again, there's room for interpretation. But Changeling isn't a game about physical manifestations of culture concepts where changing the idea landscape changes the enemy. I think it would be a different game if it were that (and there are other games that are more like what that is). It would be less personal and more zoomed out and ideological. The fundamental focus is on the relationship between changeling and Keeper, not between culture and Faerie. Culture is relevant because it is important to <i>human</i> life and speaks to what ties the Lost to the people around them ironside. To the Strangers, human life is just another performance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In a previous post, I shared my idea of a changelings titles giving a True Fae material form and wide range of abilities. I got the idea from Pennywise/It from Stephen King's <b><i>IT. </i></b>A True Fae's title's are manifestations of humanities fairytales, folklore, mythology While a title is not necessarily a True Fae's soul or psyche, it gives the True Fae rules that they have to follow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T18:46:35-07:00","id":1458599,"title":"","content":"More thoughts, there are two types of Asian American Changelings..<br /> <br /> <b><i>Eastern Court Changelings: </i></b>These are changelings of the Eastern Courts/ Asia who immigrated to the United States for some of the following reasons.<br /> 1. They are following their mortal families.<br /> 2. They are fleeing their Eastern Keeper.<br /> 3. They want to expand the power and influence of their courts.<br /> The Eastern Court changelings have discovered that with the growing Asian communities/districts in the West(China Towns, Japan Towns, Little Saigon's) Asian changelings can use the Eastern Hedge to travel to the West. Right now, this is limited only to the Eastern districts, but with the growing influence of Asia in the West, Eastern Changelings are having an easier time traveling to Europe and North America.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Western Netted Changelings: </i></b>These are Burmese, Cambodians, Chinese, Japanese, Koreans, Laotians, and Vietnamese who were captured by Western loyalists/racketeers and sold to Western True Fae. This was especially common during the Imperial European Era, Post WW2 US occupation of Japan, and the Vietnam war. It still happens, but to a MUCH LESSER degree. They usually join the seasonal court, but with Asian rituals and themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T18:57:15-07:00","id":1458602,"title":"","content":"Wait a sec. <br /> Isn\u2019t all this Culture and jazz more fitting for Beast, rather than Changeling?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T19:03:16-07:00","id":1458603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458602#post1458602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait a sec.<br /> Isn\u2019t all this Culture and jazz more fitting for Beast, rather than Changeling?</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, I think it fits better with changelings. I haven't played the Beast game, but my understanding is Beasts are humans who had their souls eaten and replaced by Monsters. Though I did play with the idea of True Fae being Beasts/Primordials who learned to manifest their full forms and abilities by drawing on human fairytales, folklore, even worship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T19:40:13-07:00","id":1458606,"title":"","content":"Well you see, Faerie entities actually don\u2019t care that much about adhering to human fairy tales etc in-universe (its us, the writers, readers, players and Storytellers that do)\u2026\u2026 but Astral entities do care, more than the Fae do, because even in-universe they <i>are</i> the human stories and legends and ideas. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s ultimately your game and your call, but that\u2019s the default assumption of the setting, I believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T21:18:48-07:00","id":1458612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458606#post1458606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well you see, Faerie entities actually don\u2019t care that much about adhering to human fairy tales etc in-universe (its us, the writers, readers, players and Storytellers that do)\u2026\u2026 but Astral entities do care, more than the Fae do, because even in-universe they <i>are</i> the human stories and legends and ideas.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s ultimately your game and your call, but that\u2019s the default assumption of the setting, I believe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Part of that is, I believe, adjusting to different eras and times. Plus, the True Fae are not limited to one title or even one form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T22:00:33-07:00","id":1458617,"title":"","content":"I feel we are kind of getting off track with the discussion on this thread, as I was hoping to share ideas for changeling chronicles that focused on Asia or Asian characters.<br /> <br /> Being a fan of Japanese folklore, especially that which focuses on the youkai, I wanted to introduce a concept that would allow the story teller to introduce and explore the many different youkai of legend. Also, influenced by Takashi Miike\u2019s \u201c<b><i>The Great Youkai War</i></b>\u201d I also wanted to introduce the themes of the chosen one, and the forces of good confronting the great forces of evil. One manga I really enjoyed was <b><i>Nurarihyon no Mago </i></b>which is about a boy who is \u00bc Youkai and the emperor/ruler of all the Yokai of Japan. Researching on Youkai wiki, I learned that the Nurarihyon IS an actual Youkai of folklore and the most powerful and ruler of youkai all over the world.<br /> <br /> The concept I came up with is the eldritch entitlement, <b><i>Nurarihyon </i></b>in which the character is essentially the emperor of ALL the Changeling courts of Japan. The privileges it provides him is that the character/player gains ALL the mantles from the courts of Japan AND can use their contacts as in court. <b><i>The Nurarihyon </i></b>also gains the powerful token/katana Nenekirimaru which acts like cold iron and deals +3 aggravated damage against faerie creatures. Against non-fae entities it does +2 lethal damage.<br /> In exchange, <b><i>The Nurarihyon\u2019s </i></b>duties include;<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Protecting the people of Japan (changelings and mortals) against the forces of the True Fae.</li> <li>Settling disputes between the different courts of Japan.</li> <li>Committing heroic deeds for the Japanese people.</li> <li>Protecting Japanese changelings from hunters and others who would torment them.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T00:05:47-07:00","id":1458623,"title":"","content":"It makes sense to me that the Changelings of Asia would have different terms for the True Fae and their servants...<br /> <br /> Terms I am considering are Asura for the Gentry/True Fae, Rakshasa for hobgoblins, and Akuma for loyalists(Yes, I am totally ripping off Kindred of the East and Exalted).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T04:41:07-07:00","id":1458648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458623#post1458623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes sense to me that the Changelings of Asia would have different terms for the True Fae and their servants...<br /> <br /> Terms I am considering are Asura for the Gentry/True Fae, Rakshasa for hobgoblins, and Akuma for loyalists(Yes, I am totally ripping off Kindred of the East and Exalted).</div> </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't such terms be mostly based on the local language? Indian changelings might use the two former terms, but why would they adopt a Japanese word for Loyalists?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T09:44:13-07:00","id":1458684,"title":"","content":"Not to mention Japanese Lost probably would call loyalists a word that means &quot;traitor&quot; or something instead of &quot;demon.&quot; As I said earlier, Kindred of the East is <i>not</i> a good model to imitate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T10:27:37-07:00","id":1458688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458648#post1458648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shouldn't such terms be mostly based on the local language? Indian changelings might use the two former terms, but why would they adopt a Japanese word for Loyalists?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True, though I do think the terms would be common in China, because of the spread of Buddhism. Do you guys have any suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T11:12:51-07:00","id":1458694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458648#post1458648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shouldn't such terms be mostly based on the local language? Indian changelings might use the two former terms, but why would they adopt a Japanese word for Loyalists?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When Japan was building its alphabet, it drew heavily on Chinese characters and China was the source of Buddhism in Japan. So some of the terms could have from the, though I DO agree most of the changeling courts would have their own local dialects and terms.<br /> <br /> In Japan for example,<br /> <br /> Youkai is a general term for Faerie creatures including changelings, hobgoblins and True Fae.<br /> <br /> Mazoku Japanese term for Gentry/True Fae.<br /> <br /> Nurarihyon: Emperor of the Japanese courts.<br /> <br /> Hyakki Yako(night parade of one hundred demons) when Nurarihyon leads the Japanese courts against the forces of the Gentry.<br /> <br /> Tsukumongami: A type of Japanese hobgoblin in which an inanimate object gains life and self awareness after 100 years in the hedge.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T12:12:47-07:00","id":1458706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458694#post1458694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Japan was building its alphabet, it drew heavily on Chinese characters and China was the source of Buddhism in Japan. So some of the terms could have from the, though I DO agree most of the changeling courts would have their own local dialects and terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of written characters are shared, but the pronunciation is completely different. (This is even true for different Chinese dialects.) For example, \u60aa\u9b54 is read in Japanese as &quot;akuma,&quot; but while it is also a word in Chinese with a comparable meaning, the Mandarin Chinese word is something like (I am not a Chinese speaker) &quot;\u00e8m\u00f3.&quot;<br /> <br /> This, incidentally, is why even Kindred of the East's &quot;native&quot; term for its titular monsters is glaringly off. &quot;Kuei-jin&quot; is clearly based on the characters \u9b3c\u4eba, but a Japanese speaker would read these characters &quot;kijin,&quot; and a Mandarin speaker would read them &quot;gu\u012dr\u00e9n&quot; (&quot;kuei&quot; and &quot;gui&quot; just being two transliterations of the same sound). You literally can't write &quot;kuei-jin&quot; with its own proper characters without outside notation.<br /> <br /> All of this also is specifically in terms of borrowing from Chinese into other languages. India does not share this relationship of borrowing from Japanese linguistically; that relationship goes in the <i>other</i> direction, though China as an intermediary. Japan might use words derived from Sanskrit, but India does not use words derived from Japanese, except maybe among pop culture fans in the modern age of anime.<br /> <br /> I still object to the idea that there would be an &quot;emperor&quot; of all the Japanese fae courts as ringing false, but I will assent that &quot;youkai&quot; is a good fit for a general Japanese term for the fae, especially inhuman fae like hobs and the Gentry.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T15:36:03-07:00","id":1458738,"title":"","content":"What Stupid Loserman said, and a little nitpicking; the idea of Nurarihyon as a leader of yokai, and the very word and concept of Mazoku, are relatively modern concepts. They\u2019d work for modern Japan, but you may want something more/else for historical settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T15:58:21-07:00","id":1458740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458706#post1458706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A lot of written characters are shared, but the pronunciation is completely different. (This is even true for different Chinese dialects.) For example, \u60aa\u9b54 is read in Japanese as &quot;akuma,&quot; but while it is also a word in Chinese with a comparable meaning, the Mandarin Chinese word is something like (I am not a Chinese speaker) &quot;\u00e8m\u00f3.&quot;<br /> <br /> This, incidentally, is why even Kindred of the East's &quot;native&quot; term for its titular monsters is glaringly off. &quot;Kuei-jin&quot; is clearly based on the characters \u9b3c\u4eba, but a Japanese speaker would read these characters &quot;kijin,&quot; and a Mandarin speaker would read them &quot;gu\u012dr\u00e9n&quot; (&quot;kuei&quot; and &quot;gui&quot; just being two transliterations of the same sound). You literally can't write &quot;kuei-jin&quot; with its own proper characters without outside notation.<br /> <br /> All of this also is specifically in terms of borrowing from Chinese into other languages. India does not share this relationship of borrowing from Japanese linguistically; that relationship goes in the <i>other</i> direction, though China as an intermediary. Japan might use words derived from Sanskrit, but India does not use words derived from Japanese, except maybe among pop culture fans in the modern age of anime.<br /> <br /> I still object to the idea that there would be an &quot;emperor&quot; of all the Japanese fae courts as ringing false, but I will assent that &quot;youkai&quot; is a good fit for a general Japanese term for the fae, especially inhuman fae like hobs and the Gentry.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree that there would be different dialects for different terms for Gentry, hobgoblins, and loyalists, though I do think certain regions might share terms. The idea of there being a Japanese changeling emperor was inspired by the Japanese imperial emperor and that I wanted the Japanese changeling courts to have their own distinct court system. When I looked up Nurarihyon on Youkai wiki, it stated that he was the ruler of all monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T16:02:33-07:00","id":1458741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458738#post1458738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Stupid Loserman said, and a little nitpicking; the idea of Nurarihyon as a leader of yokai, and the very word and concept of Mazoku, are relatively modern concepts. They\u2019d work for modern Japan, but you may want something more/else for historical settings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When I looked up Nurarihyon on Youkai wiki, it stated that he is an actual Youkai from the Okayama prefecture.<br /> <br /> Here is his description on Youkai wiki.<br /> <br /> <b>Nurarihyon</b> (\u6ed1\u74e2, <i>Nurarihyon</i>), or N\u016brihyon (\u306c\u3046\u308a\u3072\u3087\u3093, <i>N\u016brihyon</i>), is a Japanese y\u014dkai said to originate from Wakayama Prefecture. It is also sometimes believed to be descended from the <a href=\"https://yokai.fandom.com/wiki/Umib%C5%8Dzu\" target=\"_blank\">Umib\u014dzu</a> of Okayama Prefecture.<br /> <br /> Nurarihyon is a mysterious and powerful yokai encountered all across Japan. Appearances can be deceiving, and nurarihyon is the perfect illustration of that saying. Overall, he is rather benign-looking, his head elongated and gourd-shaped. His face is wizened and wrinkled, resembling a cross between and old man and a catfish. He wears elegant clothing \u2013 often a splendid silk kimono or the rich robes of a Buddhist abbot \u2013 and carries himself in the quiet manner of a sophisticated gentleman.<br /> <br /> The short, comical, elderly nurarihyon is actually the most powerful and elite of all the yokai in the world. He travels in an ornate palanquin carried by human or yokai servants, often visiting red light districts, but occasionally stopping at mountain villas as well. He is known as \u201cthe Supreme Commander of All Monsters,\u201d and every yokai listens to his words and pays him respect, treating him as the elder and leader in all yokai meetings. Along with otoroshi and nozuchi, nurarihyon leads the procession known as &quot;Hyakki Yak\u014d&quot; (the night parade of one hundred demons) through the streets of Japan on dark, rainy nights. He fits the role of supreme commander every bit as much when he interacts with humans as well.<br /> <br /> Nurarihyon shows up on evenings when a household is extremely busy. He arrives at homes unexpectedly in his splendid palanquin and slips into the house, unnoticed by anyone. He helps himself to the family\u0092s tea, tobacco, and other luxuries, acting in all respects as if he were the master of the house. His power is so great that even the real owners of the house, when they finally notice his presence, can do nothing to stop him. In fact, while he is there, the owners actually believe the nurarihyon to actually be the rightful master of the house. Eventually he leaves just as he came, quietly and politely slipping out of the house and into his palanquin, as the owners of the house obsequiously bow and wave him farewell. Only after he has left does anyone become suspicious of the mysterious old man who just visited.<br /> <br /> As to nurarihyon\u2019s origins there is only speculation, for the oldest records of his existence are mere sketches and paintings. His name connotes a slippery evasiveness \u2013 which he employs when posing as master of the house. Its name comes from \u201cnurari\u201d (to slip away) and \u201chyon\u201d (an onomatopoeia describing floating upwards) written with the kanji for gourd (due to the shape of his head).<br /> In Okayama, some evidence exists linking nurarihyon to umi-b\u014dzu. There, nurarihyon are globe-shaped sea creatures, about the size of a man\u0092s head, which float about in the Seto Inland Sea. When fisherman try to catch one, the sphere sinks down into the water just out reach and then bobs back up mockingly. It has been theorized that some of these slippery globes migrate to land, where they gradually gain influence and power, becoming the nurarihyon known throughout the rest of Japan. Whether this theory is the true origin of the Supreme Commander of All Monsters or just one more of his many mysteries is yet to be solved.<br /> <br /> You can find his entry here:<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://yokai.fandom.com/wiki/Nurarihyon\" target=\"_blank\">Nurarihyon | Yokai Wiki | Fandom</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T17:08:32-07:00","id":1458748,"title":"","content":"My discussions with 21C Hermit and Stupid Loserman are strengthening by belief that we need a 2e corebook that focuses on Asia, with different chapters dedicated to China, Japan, Korea, Vietnam, and especially the Asian American changelings, because Asians are such an important part of globalization and the history of the United States.<br /> <br /> The two types of Asian American changelings I described earlier in the thread are meant to represent the immigrant experience AND the rising influence of Asian nations like China and Japan. Thanks to globalization, the Asian courts are having an easier time traveling to the West and establishing their courts in West. They often have support groups of other Asian changelings and the Asian American communities to help them adjust to life in the West. Also, the Asia towns help provide with the sense of familiarity.<br /> <br /> The Asians who were made changelings by Western Keepers are the ones who represent the earliest immigrants from East to West AND how the immigrant experience is about suffering. In Western Arcadia, there were no images or structures to give them a sense of familiarity. Most of their fellow slaves were Westerners AND they often needed to take a crash course in English, French, and German to survive. They also needed to adapt to Western customs to avoid their Keeper\u2019s wrath. It was worse if you were your Keeper\u2019s consort in that you were often forced to act to Asian stereotypes.<br /> <br /> When they escape Arcadia, they find themselves in the West rather than the East. Worse, their country of origin has moved on without them, no longer practicing many of the customs and rituals of their human life. Because their speaking and mannerisms are now more Western rather then Eastern the Eastern court changelings often regard them with suspicion.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T20:06:45-07:00","id":1458764,"title":"","content":"The oldest instance of the supreme commander shtick with Nurarihyon is Gegege no Kitaro, AFAIK. Dated, but not old. <br /> <br /> About tying the Courts that much intimately with human culture; eh, I\u2019ve said what I needed to say. I still think its better done as a age-bound Weird Thing found in Dark Eras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T20:44:08-07:00","id":1458768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458740#post1458740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of there being a Japanese changeling emperor was inspired by the Japanese imperial emperor</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way was this idea inspired by the Japanese imperial emperor, aside from the fact that there is, indeed, a Japanese imperial emperor? &quot;Inspiration&quot; implies there are traits that you found interesting and moved you to incorporate. But you haven't described any traits of this concept. At least as presented here, it's more like saying that all the vampires in England bow to a king of all English vampires, because there is an institution of monarchy in England, and I guess for the sake of making something different for different's sake.<br /> <br /> I've probably said my piece at this point, because I don't think we're really having a conversation here and what I'm saying doesn't seem to be listened to. You're welcome to do your own thing, but I've registered my misgivings both in terms of cultural sensitivity (this is a very broad, superficial treatment of just one country's culture, and you're proposing to do it for several other countries as well) and the general presentation of Changeling: the Lost outside one's home game. If you don't agree, then my criticism isn't being helpful anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T21:30:13-07:00","id":1458775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458764#post1458764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The oldest instance of the supreme commander shtick with Nurarihyon is Gegege no Kitaro, AFAIK. Dated, but not old.<br /> <br /> About tying the Courts that much intimately with human culture; eh, I\u2019ve said what I needed to say. I still think its better done as a age-bound Weird Thing found in Dark Eras.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nurarihyon does appear in G<i><i>azu Hyakki Yagy\u014d and </i><i>Hyakkai Zukan, </i></i><i><i>two books from the Edo period. </i></i>I do think they describe him Hyakki Yako.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-04T22:35:08-07:00","id":1458783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458768#post1458768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In what way was this idea inspired by the Japanese imperial emperor, aside from the fact that there is, indeed, a Japanese imperial emperor? &quot;Inspiration&quot; implies there are traits that you found interesting and moved you to incorporate. But you haven't described any traits of this concept. At least as presented here, it's more like saying that all the vampires in England bow to a king of all English vampires, because there is an institution of monarchy in England, and I guess for the sake of making something different for different's sake.<br /> <br /> I've probably said my piece at this point, because I don't think we're really having a conversation here and what I'm saying doesn't seem to be listened to. You're welcome to do your own thing, but I've registered my misgivings both in terms of cultural sensitivity (this is a very broad, superficial treatment of just one country's culture, and you're proposing to do it for several other countries as well) and the general presentation of Changeling: the Lost outside one's home game. If you don't agree, then my criticism isn't being helpful anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>On Youkai wiki, it describes Nurarihyon as &quot;the Supreme Commander of all Monsters,&quot; I wanted him to be a changeling rather than a True Fae. I thought of how to incorporate the idea of Nurarihyon being leader of all Monsters, so what I came up with is that he is the Emperor of all Japanese changeling courts. I didn't want him to be evil and the description actually casts him in a positive light. So, drawing on <b><i>The Great Youkai War,</i></b> I used the idea of him being the one who leads the Courts of Japan against the True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T01:14:42-07:00","id":1458790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458775#post1458775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nurarihyon does appear in G<i><i>azu Hyakki Yagy\u014d and </i><i>Hyakkai Zukan, </i></i><i><i>two books from the Edo period. </i></i>I do think they describe him Hyakki Yako.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, the drawings do depict him. But the <i>interpretation</i> of \u201cthe first on standing\u201d as \u201ctop commander,\u201d as opposed to less glamorous rolls like, say, \u201cvanguard\u201d or \u201cmeat shield\u201d is the one that\u2019s modern.<br /> <br /> Granted, the Coolness factor usually outweighs such concerns\u2026 I\u2019d have him as the local Goblin Market\u2019s master, or an Entitled high-Wyrd changeling, rather than Gentry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T09:49:15-07:00","id":1458844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458790#post1458790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, the drawings do depict him. But the <i>interpretation</i> of \u201cthe first on standing\u201d as \u201ctop commander,\u201d as opposed to less glamorous rolls like, say, \u201cvanguard\u201d or \u201cmeat shield\u201d is the one that\u2019s modern.<br /> <br /> Granted, the Coolness factor usually outweighs such concerns\u2026 I\u2019d have him as the local Goblin Market\u2019s master, or an Entitled high-Wyrd changeling, rather than Gentry.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I envision is that Nurarihyon IS an Eldritch entitlement whose duties resolve settling disputes between the different changeling courts as well as disputes between Japanese mortal society and changeling society. Also, influenced by <b><i>The Great Youkai War</i></b> and <b><i>Nurarihyon no Mago</i></b> he is the one who leads that armies of the Japanese courts against the True Fae and their allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-05T15:18:29-07:00","id":1458879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1457673-asian-changeling-book?p=1458790#post1458790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, the drawings do depict him. But the <i>interpretation</i> of \u201cthe first on standing\u201d as \u201ctop commander,\u201d as opposed to less glamorous rolls like, say, \u201cvanguard\u201d or \u201cmeat shield\u201d is the one that\u2019s modern.<br /> <br /> Granted, the Coolness factor usually outweighs such concerns\u2026 I\u2019d have him as the local Goblin Market\u2019s master, or an Entitled high-Wyrd changeling, rather than Gentry.</div> </div> </div> </div>My current Nurarihyon is a fae-touched Japanese boy named Tadashi(Yes, the protagonist of <b><i>The Great Youkai War</i></b>). He becomes fae-touched when his best friend and younger sister have been kidnapped by the True Fae Susanoo. He is appraoched by a nine tailed kirsune that informs him, he is the Nurarihyon chosen by fate. He then travels into the Hedge meeting the Changeling daimyo's from around Japan and trying to unite them to help in the war against the True Fae and help rescue his friends. Through his efforts in Arcadia nad the Hedge, he gains the fairest seeming and warrior kith (a reboot of the soldier kith).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T16:05:10-08:00","id":1475370,"title":"","content":"I had previously shared interest in there being a changeling rulebook that focuses on Asia, partly because of my own fascination with Asian culture and also because Asian lore is filled with fascinating fae like creatures. There have been several comic book series that have touched on this lore and would make good sources if inspiration including <b><i>Horns,</i></b> and <b><i>My Date with Monsters.</i></b><br /> <br /> Another reason I think it would be cool to do a book that focuses on Asian changeling culture is to explore the long historical, cultural, and political connections between the Asia, and the West, especially the United States.<br /> <br /> That is why I wanted to do a Changeling chronicle to introduced three types of Asian American Changelings;<br /> 1. The Courts and Changelings from Asia that immigrated either to follow their mortal families or to build power bases in the U.S. <b>This Became MUCH more common in in the 1990's during Pax Americana </b>and Globalization began picking up steam with countries and companies expanding their business and political ties beyond their countries borders.<br /> 2. The peoples of Asia that were kidnapped and made changelings of Western True Fae. <i>This was especially common during the time of European Imperial Power, China's century of National Humiliation, and the US occupation of Japan.<b> I chose the term Cathayan for this type of Asian American Changeling, because I wanted to comment on the bias, bigotry, and stereotyping Asians have had to deal with. ALSO, </b> I felt oriental a